<!--
  Typography mockup CANDIDATE (not the picker screen) — a specimen block
  (H1, H2, body, data labels, button) using a REAL loaded webfont via
  Google Fonts. System-fallback fonts make different candidates look
  identical or wrong — this must load the actual font.

  Fill in {{GOOGLE_FONTS_FAMILY}} (the Google Fonts URL family name,
  spaces as +, e.g. "Source+Serif+4"), {{FONT_FAMILY_CSS}} (the CSS
  font-family value, e.g. "Source Serif 4"), and {{LABEL}}, delete this
  comment. When screenshotting, pass a longer wait so the webfont
  network fetch finishes first:
    capture-screenshot.sh <url> <out.png> --wait-for-timeout 1500
-->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family={{GOOGLE_FONTS_FAMILY}}:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  body { margin:0; padding:2rem; font-family:'{{FONT_FAMILY_CSS}}',sans-serif; background:#0e0e10; color:#eaeaea; max-width:520px; }
  h1 { font-size:2rem; margin:0 0 0.5rem; font-weight:700; }
  h2 { font-size:1.3rem; margin:0 0 1rem; font-weight:600; opacity:0.85; }
  p { font-size:1rem; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .data-label { font-size:0.8rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em; opacity:0.6; margin-bottom:1rem; }
  .btn { font-family:inherit; font-weight:600; background:#3a5bd9; color:#fff; border:none; padding:0.6rem 1.2rem; border-radius:6px; }
</style></head>
<body>
  <div class="data-label">{{LABEL}}</div>
  <h1>Settings</h1>
  <h2>Manage your workspace preferences</h2>
  <p>Configure notification thresholds, integrations, and default views for every project in this workspace. Changes apply immediately.</p>
  <div class="data-label">Last updated 2 hours ago &middot; 1,024 members</div>
  <button class="btn">Save changes</button>
</body></html>
